### 3️⃣ A more effective rule‑set (energy‑shaping → LQR‑like PD)

Below is a compact, deterministic policy that can be written directly into the environment’s “rule engine”.  
All constants are chosen to stay inside the allowed torque range (‑2 … 2 Nm) and to give the controller enough time to settle.

```text
# -------------------------------------------------
# 1️⃣  Decode the observation
# -------------------------------------------------
θ   ← atan2(y , x)                 # angle in [-π,π]  (0 = upright)
ω   ← angular_velocity            # already in rad/s

# -------------------------------------------------
# 2️⃣  Normalise angle so that “up” = 0
# -------------------------------------------------
if θ >  π : θ ← θ - 2π
if θ < -π : θ ← θ + 2π

# -------------------------------------------------
# 3️⃣  Energy‑shaping (swing‑up) controller
# -------------------------------------------------
# Physical constants (pendulum length = 1 m, mass = 1 kg)
g          ← 9.81
target_E   ← g * (1 - cos(0))      # = 0  (energy of the upright state)
