| **Energy‑gain `k_E = 3.0`** | Same magnitude that gave the best swing‑up in all three experiments; the factor 3 amplifies the energy error enough to push the pendulum over the top in ≈ 30–40 steps. |
| **PD‑gains (Kp = 8, Kd = 2.5)** | Identical to the balance part of the best strategy (C).  The proportional term quickly reduces the angular error, while the derivative term damps the velocity, preventing the pole from “slipping” back. |
| **Gravity‑compensation `+ g·sinθ`** | Keeps the torque from fighting gravity when the pole is already near upright, which reduces the net effort and the likelihood of saturating the actuator. |
| **Dead‑zone** | Removes the tiny torque pulses that appear when the state is already almost balanced; this cuts unnecessary energy consumption and stabilises the simulation numerically. |

