|---------|------------------|
| **Energy error** (`tau_up`) | Guarantees *just enough* energy is injected; the term `sign(theta_dot*cosθ)` avoids “pushing” when the pendulum is already moving in the right direction, reducing wasted torque. |
| **Cosine blending** (`weight`) | Removes the abrupt jump at `|θ|=0.3`.  The controller smoothly hands over torque from the swing‑up law to the PD law, preventing the occasional “‑2 N·m spike” seen in the old trace. |
| **Low‑gain PD with gravity compensation** (`tau_bal`) | Keeps `θ` and `θ̇` small with torques well inside the ±2 N·m band, dramatically lowering the `0.001*τ²` penalty once the pole is near the top. |
| **Clipping** only at the very end | Guarantees the action stays feasible while still allowing the controller to use the full torque range when it is truly needed (early swing‑up). |

