| `[0.99, 0.12, 0.68]`   | ≈ 0.12 rad (near upright) | Balancing (|θ|≤0.25 & |θ̇|≤0.8) | `‑6·0.12‑1.5·0.68+9.81·sin0.12 ≈ -0.72‑1.02+1.18 ≈ -0.56` | **‑0.56** |
| `[0.0, 1.0, 0.05]`     | ≈ π/2 rad (exactly up) | Balancing | `‑6·1.57‑1.5·0.05+9.81·1 ≈ -9.42‑0.075+9.81 ≈ 0.31` | **0.31** (tiny correction) |

The controller therefore **adds strong torque only while the pole is far from the top**, then **switches to a gentle PD** that holds the pole with minimal effort.

