| **Pendulum climbing** (`θ` moving toward 0, still outside the cone) | `u_su` stays active as long as `|θ| > θ_switch` **or** `|θ̇| > θdot_thr`. The torque magnitude shrinks automatically because `E` approaches `E_t`. | Prevents overshooting – once the pendulum has enough energy to reach the upright, the term fades out. |
| **Pendulum inside the balance cone** (`|θ| < 0.20` rad & `|θ̇| < 0.6`) | `u_su` is forced to 0, `u_pd` becomes active. The PD law quickly damps any residual motion. | The PD controller works best when the linearisation around θ = 0 is valid. Turning off the swing‑up term removes the “energy‑leak” that was causing the small constant torque in the previous runs. |
| **Any moment** | Torque is clipped to `[-2, 2]`. | Guarantees we never pay a huge penalty for a large torque; also respects the environment limits. |

